Local Debian 13 package
======================

This package follows ~/Git/btop and ~/Git/octa-capture: debhelper 13, Debian
build flags, quilt source packages and an unprivileged sbuild Trixie chroot.
It is a local maintained-fork package, not an upload to the Debian archive.
VERSION supplies the upstream version; debian/changelog supplies the revision.
Prerelease hyphens become tildes so 1.65.0~rc.1 sorts before stable 1.65.0.

The Debian binary links system libmad dynamically, unlike the standalone
release tarball. dh_shlibdeps generates its runtime library dependencies.
No libraries, services, elevated privileges or maintainer scripts are bundled.
dh_strip generates a separate optional debug-symbol package.

Install host tools:
  sudo apt install sbuild mmdebstrap uidmap devscripts debhelper lintian autopkgtest

Reuse the btop/OCTA-CAPTURE chroot, or create it once as a regular user:
  mkdir -p ~/.cache/sbuild
  mmdebstrap --mode=unshare --variant=buildd --include=ca-certificates \
    --aptopt='APT::Update::Error-Mode "any"' --arch=amd64 --format=tar \
    --skip=output/mknod trixie ~/.cache/sbuild/trixie-amd64.tar \
    'deb https://deb.debian.org/debian trixie main' \
    'deb https://deb.debian.org/debian trixie-updates main' \
    'deb https://security.debian.org/debian-security trixie-security main'

Build from the checkout, including intended uncommitted source changes:
  make deb
  # Or: python3 tools/build-debian.py --jobs 2 --output build/debian-trixie

The output directory must be new. Git-ignored files and the historical
win32/, winamp_plugin/ and makedist_win.bat payloads are excluded. The source
archive records normalized ownership and timestamps. sbuild installs only
declared build dependencies and runs the offline CTest suite in its chroot.
Checksums and build provenance are recorded in .dsc, .changes and .buildinfo.

Check and simulate installation before installing:
  lintian build/debian-trixie/*.dsc build/debian-trixie/*_amd64.changes
  autopkgtest build/debian-trixie/*.dsc \
    build/debian-trixie/streamripper_*_amd64.deb \
    -- unshare --tarball ~/.cache/sbuild/trixie-amd64.tar
  apt install --simulate ./build/debian-trixie/streamripper_*_amd64.deb
  sudo apt install ./build/debian-trixie/streamripper_*_amd64.deb

To rebuild the published source package without the Git checkout:
  dpkg-source -x streamripper_1.65.0~rc.1-1~trixie1.dsc
  cd streamripper-1.65.0~rc.1
  dpkg-buildpackage --build=binary --no-sign

The second method needs the Build-Depends from debian/control installed.
Use sbuild on the .dsc for an isolated rebuild instead. Packages are unsigned
local builds. Install with apt to resolve dependencies. Installation requires
administrator rights; recording runs as the calling user.
The autopkgtest installs the binary in a fresh rootless testbed and records
synthetic MP3 over trusted local HTTPS, checking ICY titles and Unicode names.

An older ~/.local/bin/streamripper can shadow /usr/bin/streamripper in PATH.
Use /usr/bin/streamripper explicitly to test the Debian installation.
